        IF `the person is carrying out the quality control system` AND `the person knowingly submits, or causes to be submitted, false information to the Secretary` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any person that, in carrying out the quality control system established under this subsection, knowingly submits, or causes to be submitted, false information"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `s 2025(c)(1)(C) Establishment of the liability amount`

-- The heading of (C) says "for fiscal year 2003 and thereafter"; the text says "fiscal year 2004 and any fiscal year thereafter" (NOTES.md, finding 2). The text is followed.
-- src:1952 | With respect to fiscal year 2004 and any fiscal year thereafter for which the Secretary determines that, for the second or subsequent consecutive fiscal year, a 95 percent statistical probability exists that the payment error rate of a State agency exceeds 105 percent of the national performance measure for payment error rates announced under paragraph (6), the Secretary shall establish an amount for which the State agency may be liable (referred to in this paragraph as the “liability amount”) that is equal to the product obtained by multiplying—
@ref s 2025(c)(1)(C) when the Secretary shall establish a liability amount (src:1952)
GIVEN `fiscal year` IS A NUMBER
      `the Secretary determines that, for the second or subsequent consecutive fiscal year, a 95 percent statistical probability exists that the payment error rate of the State agency exceeds 105 percent of the national performance measure` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(c)(1)(C) the Secretary shall establish a liability amount for the State agency` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the text speaks of "fiscal year 2004 and any fiscal year thereafter"
        IF `fiscal year` LESS THAN 2004 THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER `the Secretary determines that, for the second or subsequent consecutive fiscal year, a 95 percent statistical probability exists that the payment error rate of the State agency exceeds 105 percent of the national performance measure`
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any fiscal year thereafter for which the Secretary determines that, for the second or subsequent consecutive fiscal year, a 95 percent statistical probability exists"
            WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the Secretary's determination was not supplied
            OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- "the difference between the payment error rate and 6 percent" is read as the rate MINUS 0.06 (fork F-4 in NOTES.md): a rate under 6 percent gives a negative number, which the text does not address.
-- UNIT: the payment error rate is a FRACTION, not the percent printed in the text: 9 percent is 0.09, 6 percent is 0.06.
-- src:1953 | (i) the value of all allotments issued by the State agency in the fiscal year;
-- src:1954 | (ii) the difference between—
-- src:1955 | (I) the payment error rate of the State agency; and
-- src:1956 | (II) 6 percent; and
-- src:1957 | (iii) 10 percent.
@ref s 2025(c)(1)(C)(i)-(iii) the liability amount is the product (src:1953-1957)
GIVEN `value of all allotments issued by the State agency in the fiscal year, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `payment error rate of the State agency` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2025(c)(1)(C) the liability amount` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `payment error rate of the State agency` AT LEAST 0.06 THEN JUST (`value of all allotments issued by the State agency in the fiscal year, in dollars` TIMES (`payment error rate of the State agency` MINUS 0.06) TIMES 0.10)
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text does not say what a difference below zero means
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

